== Trivia ==
* The sheep color conversion spell is a reference to the priest units from [[wikipedia:Age of Empires (video game)|''Age of Empires'']], where they can turn enemy units into friendly units (changing the unit's color in the process) after making a "wololo" sound.
** Because Microsoft controls the copyrights for both ''Age of Empires'' and ''[[Minecraft]]'', [[Mojang Studios]] was able to get the actual "wololo" sound effect to use in the conversion sound effect.
* Evokers are referred to as 'evocation illagers' in the code for {{BE}}.
* Hitting an evoker in survival mode and converting the gamemode into creative mode still causes the evoker to summon fangs and vexes at the player, although they deal no damage.
* [[Vex Armor Trim]] is based on the cloak and eyebrows of the evoker.
* The texture for evokers includes a white hood. Although never used in-game, it ended up used in the book ''[[Minecraft: Maps]]'',<ref>{{Citation|url=https://www.amazon.com/Minecraft-Maps-Mojang-Ab/dp/1101966440|title=Minecraft: Maps: An Explorer's Guide to Minecraft|author=[[Mojang Studios]]|website=Amazon|date=October 8, 2019}}</ref> as well as an article on [[Minecraft.net]].<ref>{{Mcnet|meet-evoker|Meet the Evoker|May 1, 2017|[[Marsh Davies]]}}</ref>

